			"Message": "docs(Output): Restructure README with feature sections, architecture tables, and consistent emoji spacing\n\nSignificantly expand the Output README with structured documentation sections and project-convention formatting.\n\nAdded:\n- Philosophy quote block establishing Output's deterministic-build mission\n- Key Features section describing dual-compiler pipeline, plugin architecture, polyfill completeness, and service layer\n- Core Architecture Principles table mapping principles to components\n- Project Structure tree with emoji heading\n- Compatibility matrix showing target integrations\n- Prerequisites and Getting Started sub-sections\n- Funding & Acknowledgements section with 🙏🏻 emoji\n\nStandardised:\n- Em-quad spacing (&#x2001;) between all section headings and their emoji markers\n- Horizontal rules (---) between top-level sections for visual separation\n- Em-dashes (—) in place of hyphens for prose continuity\n- Bold backtick formatting for technology names (esbuild, OXC, Node.js, etc.)\n- Numbered lists converted to dashed lists with bold emphasis on key terms\n\nReorganised:\n- Architecture diagram renamed to System Architecture with connection-paths table\n- Compiler comparison and configuration options moved under In the Land Project\n- Related documentation links expanded with Sky and Wind references",
